# Design system (source of truth)

Code tokens live in `src/app/theme/tokens.js` (must stay in sync with this file’s frontmatter).  
Do not invent new colors/fonts/radii.

## Cross-platform & responsive (required)

Every new or updated UI must work on **Android and iOS**, and on **small phones and large devices (tablets)**.

- **Platforms:** Prefer React Native / Tailwind primitives that behave the same on both OS. Avoid Android-only or iOS-only layout hacks unless wrapped in `Platform.select` / `Platform.OS` with a matching fallback. Test safe areas (`SafeAreaView` / `useSafeAreaInsets`) on both notches and system bars.
- **Small screens:** Default layouts to phone widths; use flexible sizing (`flex`, `%`, `useWindowDimensions`) — never hardcode widths that clip on ~320–360dp devices. Keep horizontal padding (`px-container-mobile` / 20). Ensure text wraps; avoid fixed heights that truncate copy.
- **Tablets / large screens:** Don’t stretch phone layouts edge-to-edge into unreadable lines. Cap content width, use multi-column / centered max-width where appropriate, scale type with `headline-lg` vs `headline-lg-mobile`, and increase spacing (`stack-md` / `stack-lg`) on wide viewports. Prefer `md:` / width breakpoints via `tw` or dimension checks (e.g. width ≥ 768) over one fixed layout.
- **Touch & input:** Min touch `48` / buttons `52` on all devices; input font size ≥ 16 to prevent iOS zoom. Respect keyboard avoiding on both platforms.
- **Assets:** Images/icons must scale (`resizeMode`, responsive dimensions); no assumptions that only phone density exists.
- When creating or updating a screen/component, verify it remains usable in portrait on phones and on tablet-sized widths without overflow or sparse broken layout.
